menu "MIPI DSI Abstraction"

    config MIPI_DSI_ABSTRACTION_USE_VENDORED_ESP_HAL_LCD
        bool "Use vendored esp_hal_lcd for DSI generic read timeout detection"
        depends on SOC_MIPI_DSI_SUPPORTED
        default y
        help
            Detecting the VCOM value programmed into a MIPI DSI panel's NVM/OTP
            requires a generic/DCS read, which needs the panel to answer a bus
            turnaround (BTA) request. The DSI host has no "nobody answered"
            status bit, so upstream ESP-IDF busy-waits on the read-complete
            flags forever if no panel is attached, hanging the firmware.

            Enable this option to require the vendored esp_hal_lcd component,
            which bounds that wait with a timeout and exposes
            mipi_dsi_hal_host_gen_read_timed_out() so a missing panel can be
            detected instead of hanging.

            Disable this option to use the normal esp_hal_lcd component and
            its available functions instead. The VCOM value is still read
            correctly when a panel is attached, but without the timeout
            feature the firmware will hang if no panel is connected.

endmenu
